    <section id="game-day" class="cc-card" aria-labelledby="game-day-title">
        <h2 id="game-day-title" class="cc-section-title">Game Day &amp; Matchtrak Setup</h2>

        <div class="cc-content">
            <h3>Medical Release Forms (Red Ink)</h3>
            <p>Get a copy of the first page of each child’s registration form. Have one person listed as a guardian sign their name, in <strong>RED ink</strong>, at the bottom of their child’s form. The team’s forms will need to be at every practice, game, and team event in case of emergencies.</p>

            <h3>Game Lineup Cards</h3>
            <p>The Team Manager may prepare the lineup card, but the Head Coach is responsible for confirming it. Every team must provide a lineup card for every game. Print from Team Central and copy to region cardstock (8U and older).</p>

            <h3>Field Duty Expectations</h3>
            <ul class="cc-list">
                <li><strong>First Game of the Day (Sunshine):</strong> Paint fields, set up goals, put on nets, place sandbags, and place corner flags 1 hour before game time.</li>
                <li><strong>Last Game of the Day (Clock):</strong> Both teams break down goals and bring them to the containers along with nets and flags. Clean the trash around the fields.</li>
            </ul>

            <!-- MATCHTRAK SCORE REPORTING (COACH PAGE LANGUAGE) -->
            <h3>Inputting Match Scores After Every Match</h3>
            <span class="cc-local-rule">10U and Older Scoring Divisions</span>

            <div class="cc-callout cc-warning">
                <strong>Submit the Score Within 24 Hours</strong>
                The winning team’s Team Manager or Coach enters the final score. When a match ends in a tie, the home team’s Team Manager or Coach enters the score. Only 10U and older scoring divisions submit results.
            </div>

